  THE COMPARISON THE EVALUATION AXIS HIDES
  The DoE pipeline finishes in 3 sequential rounds. qLogEI needs 10.
  At 3 rounds qLogEI has spent only 22 of its 48 measurements (14 opening + 2 batches of 4),
  so at equal LAB TIME the comparison is not 48-vs-48 at all.
  Coordinate descent spends 48 rounds and is, on this axis, unusable in a wet lab
  regardless of its regret.

  WHAT THIS DOES NOT SHOW, stated so it is not over-read:
  E2 stored summary rows, not per-evaluation curves, so a regret-versus-ROUNDS
  CURVE cannot be drawn from the committed grid -- only the endpoint and the
  round COUNT above. Drawing the curve needs the curves persisted on a re-run.
  The round counts themselves are exact: they come from campaign.batch_plan
  and the DoE arm's own 20+27+1 split, not from a reconstruction.

  written to results/q38-cost-model.json
